Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-22-2001||10:20 PM||||I had a gf a couple year back that wanted a Boa so I surprized her and got one for her birthday. She threw it out a few days later into a dumpster cause she thought it was dead. We explained all the facts of cold blooded reptiles (and she wasnt even blonde). I got her another one from a friend who had to get rid of his, It was a few years old and about 7 or 8 feet. She liked that one. She was a real boozer and she let it run wild in the house when she was home. She passed out one nite and woke up with it curled up in a ball on her chest staring her in the face. she sold it to a store the next day!!!!!!!!! I laughed my ass off. She said it was looking mean at her.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||08-22-2001||11:34 PM||||Looking mean? Someone saying that is a sign they are scared of the snake, hell, snakes are no big deal. That seven footer has a good grip on it, but its just a big sweetheart  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||08-23-2001||12:05 AM||||I'd love a snake. As it is, I have to settle for my 6 year old Iguana named Frank. <BR>Frank's a hit with the ladies, and any small child that comes over with my parent's friends, but other than that, he doesn't do much. Eat, sleep, crap, or all three at once. He loves his heat-rock, though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
