Z||000013||Galen||08-23-2001||05:27 PM||||A baby is not natural food for snakes. 'OMG ITS A MAN EATING SNAKE' get out of the movies. I happen to know of two very domesticated snaked.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> one of mine is. Wild animals yes, so are cats & dogs. Hell, for that point so are humans. <P>Anyone who's child is 'attacked' by a python is either too stupid to own the thing, or hasn't properly taught their child not to mess with it. or both. Stupidty kills. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000014||Galen||08-23-2001||05:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>Mower said the snake had escaped from its pen. ''The little girl came across it, began to play with it and the snake restricted around her,'' he said. <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>proves my point before, stupidity kills.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Songman||08-23-2001||08:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B> proves my point before, stupidity kills.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As much as I don't want a snake in my house I have to agree with you... You really can't blame the snake. That's like blaming the gun (or the gun manufacturer) if someone shoots you. The snake is just doing what comes naturally. I have never ben afraid of snakes, but then I've never really gone out of my way to play with them either. With anything in life comes some sort of responsiblity. If you can't handle it you don't need to have it.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
